# The deep hedger's two programs: dh-fit, a Mojo program whose kernels run on
# the GPU of the image that runs it, and dh-gui, an ImGui program over SDL2.
# The compilers and the libraries are linked in and needed by no one who
# installs it.
FROM /Dollyfile-system-tools 7dc08859cff6c590c9bf42278822be15b530cc9d18438481449469995c2bf8fe
USE /demos/sdl2/Dollyfile-imgui 417da2e6fa72004a25807d4556de983a5ab91e5cf994afd8de7fbff264d772a1
USE /demos/mojo/Dollyfile-mojo 7b253fabd4d9415410267736e57cd86bbe967edc2e8e669ecfa0386a861253ff
REQUIRES HEADER libc
REQUIRES HEADER cpp
REQUIRES HEADER sdl2
REQUIRES HEADER imgui
REQUIRES LIB SDL2
REQUIRES LIB imgui
REQUIRES LIB dolly-gpu
REQUIRES TOOL c++
REQUIRES TOOL mojo
REQUIRES TOOL rm

SOURCE /dist/static/deep-hedger/dh-gui.cpp 6bc0eb6663349fa246c0b38e7735cb051ab245fb465ff2b4953e041297119899 /tmp/deep-hedger/dh-gui.cpp
SOURCE /dist/static/deep-hedger/dh-fit.mojo fcf6bdf76aeefccdff90d52ee19e6ea76b08abdd32170e94a5b76d69b345f168 /tmp/deep-hedger/dh-fit.mojo
SLOP c++ -O2 -std=c++17 -I/usr/include/imgui -I/usr/include/SDL2 /tmp/deep-hedger/dh-gui.cpp -o /usr/bin/dh-gui -limgui -lSDL2 -lm
SLOP mojo build -o /usr/bin/dh-fit /tmp/deep-hedger/dh-fit.mojo
EXPORTS TOOL dh-gui
EXPORTS TOOL dh-fit
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/dh-gui.1
    dh-gui: the deep hedger. Loads a live option chain (marketdata.app; AAPL
    needs no token), shows its bids and asks, and fits a path law to them with
    dh-fit: the model's bid and ask of every contract are what hedging its
    two sides costs along the law's paths.
    
      dh-gui                    Escape or Ctrl+C in the terminal ends it
      dh-fit CHAIN PATHS SEED   the fit alone, reporting on stdout
      dh-fit check CHAIN PATHS  its gradients against finite differences
    
    dh-fit needs gpu@0; curl fetches the chain through http@0.
